<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ada of Caria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ada was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnid-dynasty">Hecatomnid dynasty</a> of Caria, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnus">Hecatomnus</a>, who ruled as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> with her brother and husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idrieus">Idrieus</a> and alone after his death in 344 BCE. Her younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pixodarus">Pixodarus</a> drove her out around 340 BCE, leaving her only the fortress of Alinda. In 334 BCE she adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> as her son, and he restored her as ruler of Caria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ada-of-caria.jpg" alt="Ada of Caria" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marie-Lan Nguyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_of_a_colossal_statue_BM_1857.12-20.259.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
